##fileformat=VCFv4.3
##INFO=<ID=X,Extra=a>b,Number=1,Type=Integer,Description="d">
##contig=<ID=chr1,length=1000000>
##Authority=VCFv4.3.tex:117 -- "A structured meta-information line is similar, but the value is itself a comma-separated list of key=value pairs, enclosed within `<' and `>' characters" -- defines no escaping for a `>` inside an attribute value and forbids none either (VCFv4.3.tex:200's and :265's `<`/`>` exclusions are scoped to an ##ALT ID and to contig names, not to a generic attribute value). Silence, not prohibition, so warn-and-preserve is the expected outcome rather than rejection.
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1): an unescaped `>` decrements bcf_hdr_parse_line's bracket-nesting counter (`~/Dev/htslib/vcf.c:731`, "if ( *q=='>' ) nopen--;"), closing the declaration early and silently losing every later attribute -- measured live and pinned by BcftoolsDependencyTest#testUnescapedGreaterThanInMetadataValueBcftoolsTruncatesDeclaration, tabled with its own citations as STRUCTURAL_DELIMITER_HANDLING.md's Row 4 (`##contig=<ID=1,description=a>b,length=100>` truncates to `##contig=<ID=1,description=a>`, "Dropped trailing junk from header line", exit 0). This library deliberately diverges: it never treats an unquoted `>` as closing the declaration's own outer angle brackets at parse time, so Number/Type/Description all survive here; it only warns and preserves the value.
##Authority=Already-documented parse-time behavior, not a new discovery: STRUCTURAL_DELIMITER_HANDLING.md's Row 31 (written 2026-08-15) records the identical warning -- InternalUtils.parseOneAttribute's structural-character warning at InternalUtils.java:504-505 -- as a parse-time outcome. This fixture pins the same warning for the `>` trigger of the same check. VCF_SPEC_AMBIGUITIES.md's "Unquoted metadata attribute value: malformed bracket vs. `<`/`>`/`;`" entry describes a SEPARATE, EncodingProblem-based check (throws at construction, warns at validateBeforeWrite()), which is NOT what fires here; that entry's prose omitting the parse-time warning is filed in TODO.md.
##ExpectWarnContains=containing a character bcftools treats as structural; preserving it
